  "narrative": "I have appraised the results for the proposed predictive marker interactions. For Pembrolizumab, neither PD-L1 expression (H30, H31), histology (H32), nor the high-risk markers (brain metastases H33, high CRP H34, and Stage IV disease H35) showed a statistically significant or clinically meaningful interaction effect on progression-free survival. All estimates were negligible compared to the clinical significance threshold of ~0.206 (10% of the mean log_pfs). Similarly, the interaction between high NLR and the targeted therapies Sotorasib (H36), Osimertinib (H37), and Olaparib (H38) was non-significant and clinically negligible. These results suggest that the strong negative prognostic value of the inflammatory and clinical markers is independent of the treatment modality and does not serve as a predictive marker for treatment response in this dataset."
